# The definite article and every one of its sun-letter allomorphs.  Maltese
# writes il- before a moon letter, l- before a vowel, and assimilates the l to
# the following consonant when that consonant is one of the nine sun letters
# ċ, d, n, r, s, t, x, z, ż -- giving iċ-, id-, in-, ir-, is-, it-, ix-, iz-,
# iż-.  The tokenizer shears the hyphen, so each allomorph arrives as its own
# token and is listed here rather than derived.  en.wikipedia.org, "Maltese
# grammar"; memorizeinaflash.com, "Chapter 3: The Article & Basic Nouns".
il
l
iċ
id
in
ir
is
it
ix
iz
iż
